/-!
# F2b′'s successor with the joint B-set (finding: the `hull` field fails for B's own set)

Packet PROVE-AUX61-NOJUMP (round 21). **Finding (rule 1(a)).** In `Nb.SB2LowerStageVersionStatement4`, and already
in LCMEAN's `Mu.SB2LowerStageVersionStatement2`, the second line set is B's OWN filled stage set,
`A₂ t = fill (B_{≤ℓ} capped at t)`. The version field `hull` then asks
`ℍ ∖ (A₁ t ∪ A₂ t) = Φ⁻¹(ℍ ∖ relative hull at a t)`, with `A₁ t = fill (A ∪ B_{<ℓ})`. The right side is
`ℍ ∖ fill (A ∪ B_{<ℓ} ∪ B's piece up to t)`.

* **Why it fails.** If B's tail piece touches the upper prefix `A` at a point of `ℍ` before `t`, it encloses with `A`
  a pocket that lies in neither `fill (A ∪ B_{<ℓ})` (still open before the piece) nor `fill (B only)` (open through
  `A`'s position). That pocket is in the left side but not in the right side.
* **Such touches have positive probability.** B's pieces are angle-`−π/2` flow lines and `A`'s are flow lines of
  angles in `(−π/2, π/2]`. The gap is at most `π < 4π/(4 − κ) = 2λ/χ`, so they bounce off each other. In the
  relative chart, the relative piece hits the real line left of the seed (`A`'s image), where D34's heights have left
  weight `> −2`.
* **No choice of version avoids it.** The stops must cover every B-time before B's lifetime (clause (i) and `V_sup`).

**Corrected form, `Nd.SB2LowerStageVersionStatement5`:** `A₂ t` is the filled JOINT set,
`A₂ t = fill (A ∪ B_{≤ℓ} capped at t)` (the upper stage set and B's stage set through `ℓ`, capped at `t`). Then
`A₁ t ⊆ A₂ t` and `ℍ ∖ (A₁ t ∪ A₂ t) = ℍ ∖ A₂ t`, which is the pulled-back complement of the relative hull.
Every other premise and clause of `Nb.SB2LowerStageVersionStatement4` is verbatim, except that the `IsStageS2` clause is
left out (D38 moves it to PROVE-T14-SB2LIFT).
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false

noncomputable section

